# Role in the Ambient Physical AI Architecture

The Presence Layer does not identify the person and does not perform cognitive processing.

Its function is deliberately narrow:

```text
Detect human presence
        ↓
Generate a presence transition
        ↓
Notify the Identity Layer
```

System flow:

```text
Human enters the environment
        ↓
Presence Layer detects presence
        ↓
Presence Node sends presence_event
        ↓
Identity Layer requests NFC identification
        ↓
Identity Package is generated
        ↓
Cognitive Runtime receives context
```

The node therefore acts as the first physical trigger in the distributed cognitive ecosystem.

---

# Official Hardware

## Processing Unit

```text
M5Stack AtomS3 Lite
ESP32-S3
```

## Presence Sensor

```text
HLK-LD2410C
24 GHz FMCW mmWave radar
```

## Communication Between AtomS3 Lite and LD2410C

```text
UART
Baud rate: 256000
8 data bits
No parity
1 stop bit
No hardware flow control
```

Default validated pin mapping:

| Signal | AtomS3 Lite | HLK-LD2410C |
|---|---:|---|
| UART TX | GPIO1 | RX |
| UART RX | GPIO2 | TX |
| Ground | GND | GND |
| Power | according to the validated module wiring | VCC |

UART lines must be crossed:

```text
AtomS3 TX → LD2410C RX
AtomS3 RX ← LD2410C TX
```

A common ground is mandatory.

> Verify the voltage and power requirements of the exact LD2410C carrier board before connecting it. Do not assume that every carrier exposes the same regulated power input.

---

# Why the Sensor Was Changed

The original Presence Node used a VL53L0X time-of-flight distance sensor.

That implementation was important because it validated:

- ESP-IDF bring-up on the AtomS3 Lite;
- physical distance acquisition;
- threshold-based presence detection;
- the Presence State Machine;
- Wi-Fi connectivity;
- UDP broadcast;
- Presence → Identity integration.

However, distance measurement and human-presence detection are not the same thing.

The VL53L0X implementation inferred presence indirectly:

```text
Object distance
    ↓
Distance threshold
    ↓
Presence assumption
```

The LD2410C provides a more appropriate sensing model:

```text
Human movement
+
Human stationary micro-movement
    ↓
Native human-presence state
```

The migration improved the physical meaning of the Presence Layer while preserving the validated distributed architecture.

Only the sensing subsystem changed.

```text
Previous sensing subsystem:

VL53L0X
    ↓
Distance
    ↓
Threshold
    ↓
Presence
```

```text
Current sensing subsystem:

HLK-LD2410C
    ↓
Radar target state
    ↓
Presence
```

Everything after `Presence` was intentionally preserved.

---

# Preserved Architecture

The migration did not redesign the node.

The following subsystems remain compatible with the previous implementation:

- Wi-Fi Station mode;
- DHCP;
- UDP broadcast;
- UDP port `3333`;
- Presence State Machine;
- pending-event retry after network startup;
- semantic event type;
- Identity Layer integration;
- Cognitive Runtime interface.

Preserved flow:

```text
Presence Sensor
    ↓
Presence State Machine
    ↓
Wi-Fi
    ↓
UDP Broadcast
    ↓
Identity Layer
    ↓
Identity Package
    ↓
Cognitive Runtime
```

