# Component Dependencies

The LD2410 driver is included locally in the repository.

No external package manager is required for this component.

The component registration file is:

```text
components/ld2410/CMakeLists.txt
```

Content:

```cmake
idf_component_register(
    SRCS
        "ld2410.c"
        "ld2410_parser.c"
    INCLUDE_DIRS
        "include"
    PRIV_INCLUDE_DIRS
        "."
    REQUIRES
        esp_driver_gpio
        esp_driver_uart
)
```

The main component declares its dependencies in:

```text
main/CMakeLists.txt
```

Expected content:

```cmake
idf_component_register(
    SRCS "main.cpp"
    INCLUDE_DIRS "."
    REQUIRES
        ld2410
        esp_wifi
        esp_event
        esp_netif
        nvs_flash
        lwip
)
```

The `REQUIRES ld2410` entry makes the public header available to `main.cpp`:

```cpp
#include "ld2410.h"
```

The other dependencies expose the Wi-Fi, event loop, network interface, NVS and TCP/IP APIs used by the runtime.

---

# Selecting the Target

From the node directory:

```bash
idf.py set-target esp32s3
```

This command may recreate `sdkconfig`.

Run it when:

- building the project for the first time;
- the current target is not `esp32s3`;
- the build output incorrectly reports `target esp32`;
- the project was previously built for another chip.

Confirm during configuration that the build reports:

```text
Building ESP-IDF components for target esp32s3
```

---

# Clean Build

A clean build is recommended after:

- changing the target;
- adding the `ld2410` component;
- changing component dependencies;
- replacing the previous ToF implementation.

```bash
idf.py fullclean
idf.py build
```

Successful result:

```text
Project build complete.
```

The generated image is placed under:

```text
build/
```

