# End-to-End Validation

## Identity Node

Power the Identity Node and ensure it is listening on:

```text
UDP port 3333
```

The Presence Node and Identity Node must be on the same IPv4 subnet.

Example:

```text
Presence Node: 192.168.77.19
Identity Node: 192.168.77.x
Broadcast:     192.168.77.255
```

Walk into the radar detection area.

Expected Presence Node output:

```text
PRESENT
UDP presence_event sent: {...}
```

Expected Identity Layer behavior:

```text
Presence detected
Tap NFC card
```

or an equivalent log confirming receipt of the `presence_event`.

## Generic UDP Listener

A computer on the same network can also validate reception.

Example Python listener:

```python
import socket

UDP_PORT = 3333

sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)
sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)
sock.bind(("", UDP_PORT))

print(f"Listening for UDP on port {UDP_PORT}...")

while True:
    payload, address = sock.recvfrom(2048)
    print(address, payload.decode("utf-8", errors="replace"))
```

Run:

```bash
python udp_listener.py
```

Expected message:

```json
{"type":"presence_event","state":"PRESENT","distance_mm":3430,"source":"presence_node_v1"}
```

