# Troubleshooting

## `esp_wifi.h: No such file or directory`

Cause:

The `main` component does not declare the Wi-Fi dependencies.

Verify `main/CMakeLists.txt`:

```cmake
REQUIRES
    ld2410
    esp_wifi
    esp_event
    esp_netif
    nvs_flash
    lwip
```

Then run:

```bash
idf.py fullclean
idf.py build
```

## Build Uses `target esp32`

The AtomS3 Lite requires the ESP32-S3 target.

Run:

```bash
idf.py fullclean
idf.py set-target esp32s3
idf.py build
```

## Wi-Fi Disconnects With Reason `201`

Reason `201` indicates that the configured access point was not found.

Verify:

- exact SSID spelling;
- 2.4 GHz network availability;
- Wi-Fi channel and signal;
- access point visibility;
- that the correct local network is active.

## Wi-Fi Associates but No IP Appears

Expected association log:

```text
wifi:state: assoc -> run
wifi:connected with ...
```

The firmware explicitly restarts the DHCP client after association.

Wait for:

```text
Wi-Fi connected. IP: ...
Network ready: YES
```

Also verify:

- DHCP is enabled on the router;
- the subnet has available addresses;
- no MAC filtering blocks the device.

## UDP Is Postponed

Log:

```text
UDP send postponed: Wi-Fi not connected yet
```

This is expected when presence is detected before DHCP completes.

The firmware keeps one pending presence event and sends it when `wifi_connected` becomes true.

## Radar Always Reports Presence

The LD2410C detects both movement and stationary micro-movement.

Check:

- radar orientation;
- reflective or moving objects;
- fans;
- people outside the intended test area;
- module sensitivity configuration;
- installation position.

Sensor tuning is not part of this firmware baseline.

## No Radar Frames Are Received

Verify:

```text
AtomS3 GPIO1 TX → LD2410C RX
AtomS3 GPIO2 RX ← LD2410C TX
GND ↔ GND
Baud rate = 256000
```

Also verify power stability and the exact carrier-board pinout.

