# Engineering History

The Presence Layer evolved incrementally.

## V0 — CoreS3 + ToF

```text
CoreS3
+
ToF sensor
+
Arduino
```

Purpose:

- initial exploration;
- distance sensing experiments;
- proof that physical proximity could trigger ambient behavior.

Status:

```text
Historical laboratory baseline
```

## V1 — AtomS3 Lite + VL53L0X

```text
AtomS3 Lite
+
Unit Mini ToF-90 / VL53L0X
+
ESP-IDF
+
Wi-Fi
+
UDP
```

Validated capabilities:

- I²C communication;
- VL53L0X initialization;
- distance measurement in millimeters;
- threshold-based presence detection;
- hysteresis using separate present/not-present thresholds;
- Wi-Fi Station;
- UDP broadcast;
- Presence → Identity integration.

Original decision model:

```text
distance < 600 mm
        ↓
PRESENT
```

```text
distance > 800 mm
        ↓
NOT_PRESENT
```

The different thresholds reduced rapid oscillation near the decision boundary.

Status:

```text
Validated and preserved in Git history
Superseded as official sensing subsystem
```

## V2 — AtomS3 Lite + HLK-LD2410C

```text
AtomS3 Lite
+
HLK-LD2410C
+
ESP-IDF
+
Wi-Fi
+
UDP
+
Native Human Presence Detection
```

Improvements:

- native human-presence sensing;
- moving-target detection;
- stationary-target detection;
- reusable radar component;
- explicit parser and driver separation;
- preserved Presence State Machine;
- preserved UDP semantic contract;
- preserved Identity Layer integration.

Status:

```text
Official Presence Layer baseline
```

---

# Migration Decision Record

The migration followed a preservation-first rule:

```text
Replace only the sensing subsystem.
```

Changed:

- I²C removed;
- VL53L0X driver removed;
- distance thresholds removed;
- LD2410 UART driver added;
- LD2410 frame parser added;
- radar-state adapter added.

Preserved:

- Wi-Fi behavior;
- DHCP;
- UDP broadcast;
- Presence State Machine;
- semantic JSON;
- source compatibility;
- Identity Layer;
- Cognitive Runtime interface;
- repository architecture.

Success criterion:

```text
HLK-LD2410C
    ↓
Presence Detection
    ↓
Existing State Machine
    ↓
Existing Wi-Fi
    ↓
Existing UDP
    ↓
Existing Identity Layer

PASS
```

---

# Security and Deployment Notes

The current development firmware stores Wi-Fi credentials as compile-time constants.

For public release or production use, credentials should be moved to one of these alternatives:

- `menuconfig`;
- NVS provisioning;
- protected local configuration file excluded from Git;
- secure provisioning workflow.

Do not publish real SSIDs or passwords in a public repository.

Before committing, review:

```cpp
#define WIFI_SSID
#define WIFI_PASS
```

Replace private values with placeholders or an appropriate configuration mechanism.

---

# Current Scope

Implemented:

```text
Human presence detection
Moving/stationary target decoding
Presence state transitions
Wi-Fi Station
DHCP IPv4
Network status logs
UDP broadcast
Identity Layer trigger
```

Not implemented in this node:

```text
NFC identity
User profiles
LLM inference
StackFlow orchestration
MQTT
Camera vision
Ambient transformation
Expression output
```

Those responsibilities belong to other layers of the Ambient Physical AI architecture.

